<sn><md>#### Characteristics

* Developed from the `same parent material`.
* Formed under the `same climatic conditions`.
* Influenced mainly by `topography` (slope position).
* Soil properties vary `along the slope`.
* Differences in `drainage conditions`.
* Affected by `erosion and deposition`.
* Soil depth varies from `summit to valley`.
* `Soil fertility` generally increases toward the `lower slope`.
* `Water-holding capacity differs` with slope position.
* Forms a sequence of `related soils along a slope`.
